{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-soak-year-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.75, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-soak-year`: `scale-county-timeagg-soak-month`'s selections -- THC at evaporative permeation, fuel vapor venting and fuel leaks for the gasoline passenger car and light commercial truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, road types 1 and 4, January and July 2020, both day types, all 24 hours -- under `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Year\"/>`, over the same county database that STATES soakActivityFraction (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg-soak.esm`: source type 21 every month, 32 January only). MOVESOutput is 512 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is PreAggYEAR.sql's SoakActivityFraction section on top of PreAggDAY.sql's and PreAggMONTH.sql's (`scale-county-timeagg-soak-month`, PLAN.md §7.3.67): the month-collapsed stated rows are SUMMED by MonthWeighting into MonthOfAnyYear 0, `sum(soakActivityFraction x actFract)`, undivided -- MonthWeighting is the highest selected source type's monthVMTFraction (32: 0.0731 in January, 0.0923 in July), so the collapsed hot-soak plus cold-soak fraction is about 0.70 for the passenger car and 0.31 for the light commercial truck, whose January rows alone carry it -- before TankTemperatureGenerator keeps them (`mag_monthSum`). The light commercial truck HAS a Year row, unlike its July Month cell: the collapse has one month, and January's rows reach it. Permeation has no row, as at every aggregation (PLAN.md §7.3.64).\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1 and `db_aggregationmonth` the RunSpec's months (`tools/runspec-month-selection.py`). `n_outputRate` is bound to the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs of the one (county, month, day) cell, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "time-aggregation",
      "output-time-step",
      "evaporative",
      "year-aggregation"
    ]
  },
